Note: Notation IO — opt-in via `use "@notation-io"`
Note: Phase 39 D-39-01 — single-module surface for the 4 notation IO builtins:
Note:   writeMusicXML(String, Song) → Void          [Plan 39-01 XML-01]
Note:   writeLilyPond(String, Song) → Void           [Plan 39-02 LILY-01]
Note:   abc(String) → Section | Array[Section]       [Plan 39-03 ABC-01 / ABC-02]
Note:   mml(String) → Sequence                       [Plan 39-04 MML-01]
Note:
Note: Distinct from `@notation` (musical-notation primitives — note durations,
Note: rests, bar/sequence building, transitively loaded via `@std`).
Note:
Note: Round-trip CI gate for MusicXML uses `mscore --convert-to mxl` when
Note: available; charitable-skip when absent per D-39-08.

use "@std"

Note: ===== Internal C# Function Declarations =====

Note: Marker builtin called once at module load (last expression of this file).
Note: Flips ExecutionContext.NotationIoEnabled = true so the 4 surface builtins
Note: unlock. Composers should not call this directly — the trailing
Note: (__enableNotationIoModule) line below handles it for them at import time.
internal proc __enableNotationIoModule ()

Note: ----- Export builtins -----
internal proc writeMusicXML (String: path, Song: song)
internal proc writeLilyPond (String: path, Song: song)

Note: ----- Import builtins -----
Note: `abc` returns Section for single-tune input, Array[Section] for multi-tune
Note: files (≥2 `X:N` blocks). Type discrimination at runtime per D-39-16.
internal proc abc (String: source)

Note: `mml` returns Sequence (one synthetic bar containing the parsed notes;
Note: tempo populates the Sequence's MusicalContext).
internal proc mml (String: source)

Note: ===== Side-effecting init marker =====
Note: Flips ExecutionContext.NotationIoEnabled = true so the 4 builtins above
Note: unlock. Without this line, every call to writeMusicXML / writeLilyPond /
Note: abc / mml raises "requires `use \"@notation-io\"`".
(__enableNotationIoModule)
